{
  "requirement": "`Domain::source_node` maps the `OutlineId` into the graph. `Domain::node_content` returns that node’s contents. Mapping and read failures return errors. Agents use the node reference from discovery with `read_node`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.read_source.behavior`.\n\n- **`Domain::source_node` maps the `OutlineId` into the graph.** In `agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns]`, a supported `OutlineId` (`source.txt` with an empty selector) maps to the graph node `source-node`. The test checks this through the recorded `read_nodes` (`[\"source-node\", \"source-node\"]`) and the recorded `Dependency::Node(\"source-node\", fingerprint)`.\n- **`Domain::node_content` returns that node's contents.** The same test asserts `returned.format() == \"prepared contents\"`. It also checks that the record becomes stale once the domain text changes, which shows the delivered contents come from the domain.\n- **Mapping failures return errors.** The same test reads two unmappable addresses: an unknown path, and a known path with the selector `line[unknown]`. Both return an error containing \"unsupported source item\". No dependencies are recorded and the domain read count stays 0, so the read is never attempted.\n- **Read failures return errors.** The same test sets `fail_read = true` for a supported id. It asserts the error \"prepared source read failed\" and that no dependency is recorded. A successful read afterwards records one dependency.\n- **Agents use the node reference from discovery with `read_node`.**\n  - In `agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions]`, a `list_sources` result supplies the node reference. `read_node` with `\"unknown\"` is rejected with \"unknown node\". `read_node` with the listed node returns the domain's \"a source snapshot\" and not the on-disk \"selected disk contents\". The `search_text` hit's `node` is also passed to `read_node` (turn 14), and the test runs two independent executions.\n  - Other tests in `agent/tests.rs` exercise the `read_source` path: `source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results`, `source_tools_keep_search_discovery_separate_from_delivered_source_reads`, `source_reads_track_optional_dependencies_and_empty_searches_remain_discovery`, `cached_selected_source_reads_record_exact_delivered_contents_and_errors_add_no_input` and `source_read_pages_retain_text_and_dependencies_without_another_read`. They cover several selector forms, delivered text and dependency recording.\n  - `agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[search_excerpts_redact_credentials_before_serialization_and_paging]` checks that discovery does not read the domain (`reads == 0`).\n\nI found no plausible behavior that violates the requirement and that these tests would accept.",
